================================================================================
         ROV TELEMETRY GROUND STATION - DAM INSPECTION MISSION CONTROL
       Coratia Technologies Software Internship Technical Assessment
================================================================================

A native cross-platform desktop application built with Python & PySide6 (Qt)
simulating an underwater dam inspection ROV deployed at Nagarjuna Sagar Dam.


================================================================================
1. HOW TO RUN THE APPLICATION (BY OPERATING SYSTEM)
================================================================================

Choose your operating system below to start the ground station immediately:

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[WINDOWS]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method A (Easiest - 1 Click):
    Simply double-click the file:
      scripts\run_windows.bat

  Method B (Via Command Prompt or PowerShell):
    Open your terminal in this project folder and run:
      python -m venv venv
      venv\Scripts\activate
      pip install -r scripts\requirements.txt
      python main.py

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[LINUX / UBUNTU]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method A (Easiest - 1 Click Script):
    Open your terminal in this project folder and run:
      ./scripts/run_linux.sh

  Method B (Via Terminal manually):
    python3 -m venv venv
    source venv/bin/activate
    pip install -r scripts/requirements.txt
    python3 main.py

  Method C (Pre-compiled Standalone Binary):
    If using the standalone build, you can launch it directly without Python:
      ./dist/ROVGroundStation/ROVGroundStation


================================================================================
2. PILOT CONTROLS (KEYBOARD & JOYSTICK)
================================================================================

IMPORTANT: When the station opens, the vehicle is in a safe "DISARMED" state.
Click the red [DISARMED] button in the top bar to ARM thrusters before flying.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Keyboard Flight Controls:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * UP ARROW (^)    : Surge Forward (pushes ROV forward up to 1.8 m/s)
  * DOWN ARROW (v)  : Surge Reverse (pushes ROV backward)
  * RIGHT ARROW (>) : Strafe Right (lateral sway up to 1.2 m/s)
  * LEFT ARROW (<)  : Strafe Left (lateral sway)
  * S KEY           : Dive (pushes vertical thrusters downward)
  * W KEY           : Surface / Ascend (rises toward surface 0.0m)
  * D KEY           : Turn Right / Clockwise (yaw rotation)
  * A KEY           : Turn Left / Counter-Clockwise (yaw rotation)

  Note on Key Behavior:
    - Holding any flight key drives the ROV continuously.
    - Releasing the key cuts motor power and water drag stops the ROV promptly.
    - If unpressed for 1.0 second in Manual mode, the safety watchdog auto-cuts
      all manual thrust to zero.
    - Multi-key combinations (e.g., UP + RIGHT for diagonal movement) work
      simultaneously.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
USB Gamepad / Joystick Flight Controls (Plug-and-Play):
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Left Stick (Y-axis)  : Forward / Reverse
  * Left Stick (X-axis)  : Strafe Left / Right
  * Right Stick (Y-axis) : Dive / Surface
  * Right Stick (X-axis) : Turn Left / Right
  * Button A (Cross)     : Arm / Disarm Toggle
  * Button B (Circle)    : Quick Release to Manual Mode


================================================================================
3. AUTOPILOT MODES & MISSION CONTROLS
================================================================================

The Ground Station supports 3 primary operational modes:

1. MANUAL MODE (100% Pilot Control):
   Direct joystick or keyboard driving with active water drag deceleration.
   Thrusters auto-cut after 1 second of operator inactivity.

2. DEPTH HOLD MODE (Closed-Loop Vertical Autopilot):
   - Type your desired target depth in the "Target Depth" box (e.g., 10.0 m)
     and click [ENGAGE DEPTH HOLD], or select DEPTH_HOLD from the dropdown.
   - Closed-loop proportional-derivative (PD) controller locks vertical depth.
   - Even if strong downward spillway currents push the vehicle, vertical
     thrusters dynamically adjust to keep the ROV locked at the exact target.
   - While Depth Hold is active, you can still steer forward/back/left/right,
     or use W/S to smoothly nudge the target depth.

3. HEADING HOLD MODE (Closed-Loop Compass Direction Autopilot):
   - Type your target compass heading in degrees (0 to 359) and click
     [ENGAGE HEADING HOLD].
   - Autopilot automatically fires differential yaw thrusters to align the
     nose of the ROV with the requested heading and resist rotational drift.
   - While Heading Hold is active, you can still drive forward or dive.

4. DUAL HOLD (DEPTH & HEADING HOLD):
   Both closed-loop controllers run simultaneously, holding both depth and
   orientation while allowing manual horizontal translation.


================================================================================
4. KEY FEATURES & DASHBOARD MODULES
================================================================================

1. SUBSEA WATER COLUMN CROSS-SECTION (2D Live Canvas):
   - Custom real-time visual canvas rendering the surface waves and the
     Surface Support Boat (GPS Anchor) floating at 0.0m.
   - Umbilical tether cable connects the surface vessel to the underwater ROV.
   - Dynamic auto-scaling depth ruler that smoothly adjusts from surface to
     deep water (up to 100m).
   - Live gold dashed setpoint line showing target depth during Depth Hold.
   - Real-time forward headlights illuminate murky reservoir water.

2. LIVE DEPTH-VS-TIME PROFILE CHART:
   - Hardware-accelerated dynamic real-time depth graph (pyqtgraph).
   - Inverted depth axis (0m surface at top, diving down).
   - Cyan dashed Surface (0m) reference line and dynamic Target Depth setpoint.
   - Time axis locked in standard SI seconds (s).

3. HIGH-RESOLUTION OFFLINE MAP (Nagarjuna Sagar Dam Reservoir):
   - Positioned directly over Nagarjuna Sagar Dam (16.579554 N, 79.312759 E).
   - 100% OFFLINE operation using pre-cached local map tiles (no internet needed).
   - Two selectable layer options:
       * "Satellite"  : High-resolution satellite imagery (default).
       * "Street Map" : OpenStreetMap street/reservoir topographic view.
   - Live GPS coordinate display, compass heading, and live support boat anchor.

4. SIMULATED WATER CURRENT (Hydrodynamic Environmental Drift):
   - 4 selectable river current speed presets:
       * Calm (0.0 m/s)
       * Mild (0.3 m/s)
       * Moderate (0.7 m/s)
       * Strong (1.2 m/s)
   - Compass flow direction selector (East 90 deg, SE 135 deg Spillway, etc.).
   - Optional Spillway Downdraft (0.25 m/s suction) to test autopilot response.

5. SUBSEA 5S LI-ION BATTERY SYSTEM:
   - Modeled after real-world subsea robotics power packs: 5S Li-ion/NMC
     (21.0V Full, 18.5V Nominal, 15.0V Cutoff limit).
   - Real-time dynamic load-based drain: power draws faster when thrusters fire.
   - Color-coded voltage badge with percentage calculation.

6. SAFETY WATCHDOG & INTERLOCKS:
   - Disarmed Lock: Propellers are strictly cut to 0% power when Disarmed.
   - Prominent red alert banner warns operator whenever the vehicle is disarmed.
   - 1.0-second inactivity watchdog neutralizes thrust if keyboard is released.


================================================================================
5. SOFTWARE ARCHITECTURE (CLEAN MVC PATTERN)
================================================================================

The codebase follows strict Model-View-Controller (MVC) separation:

* MODEL (src/rov_simulator.py):
  - Pure Python physics engine independent of any GUI libraries.
  - Simulates full 6-DOF underwater kinematics (Surge, Sway, Heave, Roll,
    Pitch, Yaw): provides active thruster driving for Surge, Sway, Heave,
    and Yaw, with passive metacentric self-righting stability maintaining
    Roll and Pitch level at 0.0°.
  - Implements motor lag (exponential filter), water resistance drag damping,
    environmental river currents, battery discharge, and closed-loop PD
    controllers for depth and heading hold.

* VIEW (src/view/ modular package):
  - src/view/dashboard.py      : Master window shell and 20 Hz event coordinator.
  - src/view/top_bar.py        : Arm switch, mode selector, hold setpoint controls.
  - src/view/left_panel.py     : Primary telemetry speeds, thruster gauges, keymap.
  - src/view/right_panel.py    : 2D water column, depth plot, offline map.
  - src/view/custom_widgets.py : SubseaWaterColumnWidget (QPainter) & CleanSpinBox.
  - src/view/title_bar.py      : Frameless title bar with window controls.
  - src/view/resources.py      : Cross-platform asset path resolution.

* CONTROLLER (main.py):
  - Initializes the application and runs a synchronized 20 Hz (50 ms) loop.
  - Polls pilot inputs, steps the physics model, and pushes fresh telemetry
    to all visual components.


